{
  "unit": {
    "id": "9",
    "title": "Whose is it?",
    "blurb": "The genitive: of the boy, of the boys",
    "intro": "The genitive case says who owns something or who is related to someone. It is the “'s” of English: _liber puerī_ (the boy's book), _liber puerōrum_ (the boys' book), _fīlia Mārcī_ (Marcus's daughter). First-declension genitive: _-ae_ (singular), _-ārum_ (plural). Second declension: _-ī_ and _-ōrum_. Third declension: _-is_ and _-um_. _Cuius?_ asks “whose?”."
  },
